      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T06:17:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"If there are multiple writers it\u0027s possible that the tpm task can hit this path from its tpm_reset_now()\"\n\nno, other writers will not be able to write, they will have to wait on the mutex in nvmem_write(). Or the tpm task will have to wait on the mutex when it invokes \"nvmem_write\", but it will not come here without acquiring the lock first.",
      "revId": "de820f11555a548f437b84b1ca4df600a3911b92",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a1275fb_796c4316",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 575,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T06:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Somehow we need to assert our assumptions w.r.t. single writer and user.\n\nThe reason is this:\ntask A writes and commits(), but !commits_enabled.\ntask B tries to write but can\u0027t because the commit never went through nvmem_save() which releases the lock.\n\nif task B is the TPM task (currently only one that can enable them) then we are dead locked because the TPM task is waiting on the mutex that is unreleased by A.",
      "revId": "de820f11555a548f437b84b1ca4df600a3911b92",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "525e620b_89c9cc94",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 584,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T05:27:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this becomes quite the problem when commits are not enabled. We\u0027ve backed up all readers. I\u0027m not sure if if we are doing nvmem reads from other tasks than the TPM, but once a write is done and we\u0027ve disable commits temporarily those other tasks are blocked.\n\nIn a previous comment you said:\n\"It is not limited. If there is no write in progress - any number of tasks can read, each read enveloped in grabbing/releasing the mutex.\nIf a task writes something - only it can read or write until commit happens, all other taks\u0027 attempts to read or write will be stalled by the mutex.\"\n\nIf there are multiple writers, we have code paths where this function is called from the TPM task. We could fail the !\u003d task_get_current() check. What\u0027s worse is that there are a lot of global variables in this module with no protection. So are there multiple writers? If so, then there\u0027s a lot things that can break down.",
      "revId": "de820f11555a548f437b84b1ca4df600a3911b92",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f978c90_c8c34cab",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 584,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T05:43:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "well, I am not introducing the locking scheme in this patch, I am actually improving it. Before this only one task could both read and write until the commit happens.\n\nThere are global variables in this module, but they are touched only when the task is trying to write, and this can happen only after lock is obtained.\n\nYes, if two or more tasks want to write concurrently, it could be an issue, i.e. the tasks other than the first one will have to wait.  I don\u0027t know a way around it, do you have a suggestion?",
      "revId": "de820f11555a548f437b84b1ca4df600a3911b92",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aeed92c5_6a5d114d",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 584,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T05:57:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Global variables being set without any protection where any task can be pre-empted is prone to hitting bugs. As I noted before nvmem_commit() can be called from the tpm task by way of nvmem_enable_commits(). Previously you said reads and writes were from a single task. If that\u0027s not the case this code needs to be fixed.",
      "revId": "de820f11555a548f437b84b1ca4df600a3911b92",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
